{"description": "🐠 Babel is a compiler for writing next generation JavaScript.", "homepage": "https://babel.dev", "topics": [], "pushed_at": "2026-11-09T19:20:47Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-09T20:26:37Z", "detail": {"avatar": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9637642?v=4", "license": "MIT", "discussions_total": 546, "latest_release": {"name": "", "tag": "v8.1.1", "published_at": "2026-11-02T12:53:35Z", "body": "## v8.1.1 (2026-11-02)\r\n\r\nThis release includes `@babel/plugin-proposal-bytes-modules`, `@babel/plugin-proposal-filtered-namespaces`, and `@babel/plugin-proposal-text-modules`, which were accidentally excluded from 8.1.0."}, "hot_issues": [{"number": 8309, "title": "Babel 7 ignores files outside of project directory", "comments": 51, "created_at": "2018-07-12T12:13:47Z"}, {"number": 5357, "title": "transform-react-inline-elements causes duplicate react error", "comments": 30, "created_at": "2017-02-22T01:11:24Z"}, {"number": 6637, "title": "Features support data source", "comments": 26, "created_at": "2017-01-04T17:26:23Z"}, {"number": 9540, "title": "generateExpression (no trailing semicolon)", "comments": 25, "created_at": "2019-02-18T21:52:21Z"}, {"number": 7357, "title": "injecting external-helpers in a node app", "comments": 25, "created_at": "2018-02-08T20:49:23Z"}, {"number": 3977, "title": "CLI (babel init) command to guide people through setting up Babel (T6956)", "comments": 25, "created_at": "2016-01-13T03:42:37Z"}, {"number": 6931, "title": "Bug: wrong unicode regexp", "comments": 24, "created_at": "2017-11-29T22:21:04Z"}, {"number": 12208, "title": "Make JSX pragmas override the configured runtime mode", "comments": 22, "created_at": "2020-10-18T08:46:52Z"}], "discussions": [{"number": 18495, "title": "v8.1.0", "comments": 0, "category": "Releases", "created_at": "2026-11-02T12:41:35Z"}, {"number": 18321, "title": "npm provenance attests the commit before the release commit, so the attested tree never contains the published version", "comments": 2, "category": "Releases", "created_at": "2026-10-07T19:03:53Z"}, {"number": 18164, "title": "Not all babel packages have a v8 released yet. Will they get one?", "comments": 1, "category": "General", "created_at": "2026-08-03T03:28:05Z"}, {"number": 18163, "title": "Documentation : v8 CLI file glob sort order changed", "comments": 2, "category": "General", "created_at": "2026-08-01T12:07:44Z"}, {"number": 18146, "title": "After migration to Babel 8, babel gets confused by the generic syntax in .ts files", "comments": 1, "category": "Q&A", "created_at": "2026-07-20T14:29:03Z"}, {"number": 18124, "title": "Babel 8 noop removal, how do I adjust?", "comments": 2, "category": "Q&A", "created_at": "2026-07-08T18:20:32Z"}, {"number": 18110, "title": "New Member", "comments": 0, "category": "General", "created_at": "2026-06-30T04:01:33Z"}, {"number": 18072, "title": "v8.0.0", "comments": 0, "category": "General", "created_at": "2026-06-16T14:04:26Z"}], "readme_excerpt": "<p align=\"center\">\n  <a href=\"https://babeljs.io/\">\n    <img alt=\"babel\" src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/babel/logo/master/babel.png\" width=\"546\">\n  </a>\n</p>\n\n<p align=\"center\">\n  The compiler for writing next generation JavaScript.\n</p>\n\n<p align=\"center\">\n    <a href=\"https://npmx.dev/package/@babel/core\"><img alt=\"npm Downloads\" src=\"https://img.shields.io/npm/dm/@babel/core.svg?maxAge=43200&label=npm%20downloads&logo=babel&logoSize=auto\"></a>\n</p>\n<p align=\"center\">\n  <a href=\"https://github.com/babel/babel/actions/workflows/ci.yml\"><img alt=\"GitHub CI Status\" src=\"https://github.com/babel/babel/actions/workflows/ci.yml/badge.svg?branch=main\"></a>\n  <a href=\"https://codecov.io/github/babel/babel\"><img alt=\"Coverage Status\" src=\"https://img.shields.io/codecov/c/github/babel/babel/main.svg?maxAge=43200&logo=codecov\"></a>\n  <a href=\"https://pkg.pr.new/~/babel/babel\"><img alt=\"pkg.pr.new\" src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/PR_previews-pkg.pr.new-10a5e9\"></a>\n</p>\n<p align=\"center\">\n  <a href=\"https://slack.babeljs.io/\"><img alt=\"Slack Status\" src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/chat-on_slack-brightgreen?style=flat&logo=slack&logoColor=white\"></a>\n</p>\n\n<h2 align=\"center\">Supporting Babel</h2>\n\n<p align=\"center\">\n  <a href=\"#backers\"><img alt=\"Backers on Open Collective\" src=\"https://opencollective.com/babel/backers/badge.svg\" /></a>\n  <a href=\"#sponsors\"><img alt=\"Sponsors on Open Collective\" src=\"https://opencollective.com/babel/sponsors/badge.svg\" /></a>\n  <a href=\"https://medium.com/friendship-dot-js/i-peeked-into-my-node-modules-directory-and-you-wont-believe-what-happened-next-b89f63d21558\"><img alt=\"Business Strategy Status\" src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/business%20model-flavortown-green.svg\"></a>\n</p>\n\nBabel (pronounced [\"babble\"](https://soundcloud.com/sebmck/how-to-pronounce-babel))  is a community-driven project used by many companies and projects, and is maintained by a group of [volunteers](https://babeljs.io/team). If you'd like to help support the future of the project, please consider:\n\n- Giving developer time on the project. (Message us on [Twitter](https://twitter.com/babeljs) or [Slack](https://slack.babeljs.io/) for guidance!)\n- Giving funds by becoming a sponsor on [Open Collective](https://opencollective.com/babel) or [GitHub](https://github.com/sponsors/babel/) (which goes to our Open Collective account)!\n\n## Sponsors\n\nOur top sponsors are shown below! [[Become a sponsor](https://opencollective.com/babel#sponsor)]\n\n<a href=\"https://opencollective.com/babel/sponsor/0/website\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://opencollective.com/babel/sponsor/0/avatar.svg\"></a>\n<a href=\"https://opencollective.com/babel/sponsor/1/website\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://opencollective.com/babel/sponsor/1/avatar.svg\"></a>\n<a href=\"https://opencollective.com/babel/sponsor/2/website\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://opencollective.com/babel/sponsor/2/avatar.svg\"></a>\n<a href=\"https://opencollective.com/babel/sponsor/3/website\" target=\""}}